------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  HEADLINE (node): 0.990x on the 118,559 positions that MOVED.
  The pooled 1.010x includes 343,551 flat positions (74%) where persistence
  is exact by construction and no forecast can do better than tie.
  LADDER : 1.031x vs shrink(alpha=0.990) -- does NOT beat the shrinkage oracle.  (1.028x vs persistence, n=250,427)
  MECE   : 0.853x vs shrink(alpha=0.917) -- BEATS the shrinkage oracle.  (0.819x vs persistence, n=41,700)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  An alpha well below 1 means the quantity genuinely mean-reverts and there
  is something for a forecaster to find; an alpha near 1 means it is a random
  walk and beating persistence on it would be surprising. That difference --
  MECE alpha ~ 0.87 against ladder alpha ~ 0.99 -- is the structural finding,
  and it follows from the constraints themselves: a MECE basket is pinned to
  a LEVEL (the legs must sum to 1), while a ladder pair is only bounded by an
  INEQUALITY (gap <= 0), which an entire half-line satisfies. There is no
  level for a ladder gap to revert to, so there is nothing to forecast.
